    "body": "Preserve the accepted v0.2.0 mathematics and release while adding always-on source, exact TeX-export and archival restoration gates. Accepted authority A remains d8a4ffb5b63eb9359a4c0af9134b4f9a3c529618; current main/base B is merged contract PR #78 at 37c0cb8f2fbe7934639127e5f8b6d64a01e6950f.\n\nCurrent head H: 92e45179a5e3ecbe1b2bcadc4da54a0d1657f501. Tooling T: 71cc34fa0bc4b639c05d2ec5f39f0b88afd56388. Supplement: 71 files/35 tooling and guide entries; 36 historical refs, 26 input commits and 8,202 objects. Publication-candidate ZIP: 7,465,148 bytes; SHA-256 f6f119cadb1a3ebe09f9010510476bab2e75194ededde922eb99a8891652eca4. Manifest SHA-256 8fc56980228519e96e927a212b3c49afbebd5007ef8f1fa3086b17241a3da18d.\n\nAll 17 reported Codex threads across PRs #77/#78 have dispositions: 16 valid findings fixed; one ancestry claim rebutted against the actual immutable PR head/synthetic and successful archive job, preserving the ancestor requirement. Latest fixes bind all five legacy required jobs to genuine current-HEAD PR/main-push contexts before verification, retain source artifacts, pin the complete reviewed 19-workflow set against name collisions, verify the committed ZIP/sidecar against every canonical supplement file, and enforce traversal/count/aggregate budgets before hashing. Independent repaired-hash/metadata attacks reach their intended validators. Clean-T full workflow suite: 8 methods PASS.\n\nExact-H independent package review passes all 369 frozen entries, full T/C/executing/guide closure, publication ZIP contents/metadata, all workflow profiles and zero Lean/release/frozen-source changes. Bundle encoding changed to SHA-256 f49203e5a7f2189565c24509bd56652318ab383dfcda36ee756b78332b1e5792 (6,639,932 bytes); refs/object inventories are byte-identical. A fresh empty local import, strict fsck, exact 8,202-object closure and complete parent/tree/ancestry bindings passed. That local run was not network isolated and did not replay legacy tools or run Lean. Fresh genuine synthetic CI must perform those separate stages before acceptance; previous-head green results are historical only.\n\nNo new/changed theorem declarations or assumptions, Lean trees/roots, toolchain, application schema or accepted release bytes. Strict MA2 and existing A3/D2/E1/X1 limits remain unchanged. All 108 requirements retain their IDs/levels: 87 unit, 2 integration, 6 live-PR, 1 review, 12 separately authorized OPS. Reviewer and publication destination remain undetermined. Settings, archival tags and external publication remain deferred by the user. The repository ZIP is a publication candidate, not external publication. Final source-bound acceptance will be pushed separately to avoid self-reference.",
